Rewritten: the five OpenRouter calls the plugin made — Decisions, Extractions,
Rerank, Embeddings and the web_search server tool — as five verbs in the
OPENROUTER-EVERYTHING package and five model-facing tools, each speaking
OpenRouter's REST API directly from Common Lisp, with the plugin's curated
default model per capability as the fallback when the config names none, its
/api/alpha derivation from the configured /api/v1 base, its attribution
headers, and its key order (api_key, then the named variable, then
OPENROUTER_API_KEY). Left out: the plugin was a Hermes provider plugin, so it
also registered web search/fetch, image generation, video generation, TTS and
STT as Hermes providers and rewrote Hermes' config.yaml to switch them on.
A Nodecode provider lane is a different cell's job — OpenRouter's chat lane
and its voice APIs already have cells — so this one keeps the calls that are
verbs rather than lanes, and the per-capability model choice survives as the
section's *_model members instead of a config rewrite. Also left out: the
plugin's model-adequacy validator, which read Hermes' live model catalog to
reject a mismatched model; a section naming a model by hand has no such
switch to guard.
